MID_LGV_1SEO_c01_LG13_001_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c01_LG13_001_m01_001: Thinking on it, I have not been here in the royal\npalace of Megaira for some time.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c01_LG13_001_m01_002: Perhaps you should reacquaint yourself with the\npeople here before meeting with King Sergio.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c01_LG13_001_m01_003: I am sure many of them have been eagerly awaiting\nyour return, Your Highness.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c01_LG13_001_m01_004: That is a fine idea. I shall mingle here before\nproceeding to {SetColor=Gold}my father's chambers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c02_GM13_001_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c02_GM13_001_m01_001: There is not a moment to waste. We must make\nhaste for Megaira.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c02_GM13_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c02_GM13_002_m01_001: Whew! You had us worried, but at least we found\nyou soon enough.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c02_GM13_002_m01_002: Indeed. Let us renew our focus and set our sights\non Megaira.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_002_m01_001: This is the guesthouse assigned to us. It will serve as\nour base of operations while in Dagsion.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_002_m01_002: We have some time before our audience with the\nDivine Sovereign. I should {SetColor=Gold}inspect our quarters{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_002_m01_003: As you wish, Your Majesty. {SetColor=Gold}Inform me when you\nare ready{SetColor=Default}, and we can proceed to the audience.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_003_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_003_m01_001: First things first—I want to see Aurora. Let us not\ndelay in proceeding to {SetColor=Gold}her temple{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_005_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_005_m01_001: Ooh, so this is the famous Temple Row! It's really\nsomething to see all the grand entrances lined up.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_005_m01_002: But, uh...which one is Aurora's?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_005_m01_003: It's right over there. You can see the {SetColor=Gold}entrance to\nAurora's temple{SetColor=Default} from here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_001: So then, where is Yu Phas's temple?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_002: Haha! It is just ahead, directly across from us.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_003: Though to judge by the guard posted there, access to\nthe temple has been prohibited.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_004: And judging by our experience at Aurora's temple,\nI doubt they will make an exception for us.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_005: If I could not have an audience with Aurora, I would\nat least like to visit Yu Phas's temple.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m01_006: Though it does seem barred to us. Let us see if we\ncan spot {SetColor=Gold}another entrance{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m02_001: Hmm. That walkway extends from the spot the\ngatekeeper was guarding.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m02_002: So it does, now that you mention it.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m02_003: Meaning that if we can get up to {SetColor=Gold}the walkway{SetColor=Default},\nwe can access the temple.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c03_LG13_006_m02_004: Hmm...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_001: Bonaventure, I would hear your thoughts on\na certain matter.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_002: I am, as ever, at your service.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_003: With the new additions to our clan, I feel certain of\nour victory in the Heroic Games. And yet...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_004: There is time on our hands, and I believe we ought\nnot to let it go to waste.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_005: A splendid idea. Might I suggest attempting a\n{SetColor=Gold}certification exam{SetColor=Default}?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_006: Did you just say "exam"? I dunno...I'm pretty old\nto go back to school.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_007: Certification exams are a tried-and-true system\nemployed by the temples for ages.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_008: {SetColor=Gold}Pass{SetColor=Default} them to be authorized to {SetColor=Gold}explore a variety\nof classes{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_009: The most important criteria in these exams are the\nmartial skills required for each class.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_010: If your {SetColor=Gold}skills {SetColor=Default}are at the {SetColor=Gold}appropriate level{SetColor=Default}, you ought\nto {SetColor=Gold}pass {SetColor=Default}the exam with ease.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_011: So no homework? We just gotta go around fighting\nto build up our skills?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_012: Precisely. And it needn't be actual combat. We can\nhone the requisite skills at the {SetColor=Gold}training grounds{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_013: I was unaware of these training grounds. Where\nmight one find them, Bonaventure?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m01_014: They are part of the {SetColor=Gold}colosseum{SetColor=Default} in {SetColor=Gold}midtown{SetColor=Default}. If you\nare interested, by all means avail yourself of them.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_Closed_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_Closed_m01_001: The colosseum ought to be at the bottom of the stairs\nto Temple Row.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_Closed_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_Closed_m02_001: Er, Your Majesty, we are going a bit astray from\nthe colosseum.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m02_001: I am told that I can receive training here. Is it so?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m02_002: You heard right. Want to sign up?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m02_003: Yes. And though it is short notice, I should like to\nbegin right away.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m02_004: There is a {SetColor=Gold}fee for the service{SetColor=Default}, Your Majesty. I took\nthe liberty of bringing it this time.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m03_001: I am told that I can receive training here. Is it so?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m03_002: You heard right. Though y'know, you {SetColor=Gold}can't go in\nthere alone{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m03_003: Pardon? Hmm. I shall need a partner, then.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m04_001: You're Queen Theodora, yeah? I'll join you, if you\ndon't mind.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m04_002: By all means. I would very much appreciate it.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_108_m04_003: Since it's your first time using the training grounds,\nI'll waive the fees. But just this once.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m01_001: Now that you have honed your skills, the time is\nright for a {SetColor=Gold}certification exam{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m01_002: You will find the {SetColor=Gold}proctor{SetColor=Default} who administers them at\nthe very top of Temple Row.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_Closed_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_Closed_m01_001: Pardon me, Your Majesty, but this is not the way to\nour destination.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_WrongPerson_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_WrongPerson_m01_001: Ah, that is not the proctor, Your Majesty. Speak to\nthe other one here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m02_001: What gives? Now we need a {SetColor=Gold}license{SetColor=Default} to take a\ncertification exam?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m02_002: Indeed. Typically, one would purchase them from the\n{SetColor=Gold}license vendor{SetColor=Default} nearby.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m02_003: This time, though, I procured one in advance. It is\nyours to use on a certification exam.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m03_001: I believe I have a grasp on the overall process.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_109_m03_002: Shifting to {SetColor=Gold}new classes{SetColor=Default} will {SetColor=Gold}strengthen our forces{SetColor=Default}.\nIt will be key to realizing our long-held dream.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m01_001: This may interest you, Your Majesty...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m01_002: Out with it, then.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m01_003: I have confirmed and reconfirmed it with the\norganizers of the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m01_004: But it seems that the use of {SetColor=Gold}battalions{SetColor=Default} is not against\nthe rules of the contest.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m02_001: That's great! If we get battalions, then {SetColor=Gold}we get to use\ngambits{SetColor=Default} too. We'll be unstoppable!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m02_002: It would be an effective way to demonstrate our\nprowess to onlookers. Let us employ one right away.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m02_003: I thought you might say that, and so I have already\nput a battalion together. It is at your command.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m03_001: A battalion must first be assigned before it can be\nused. Do so from {SetColor=Gold}Assign {SetColor=Default}under {SetColor=Gold}Inventory{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m04_001: I like the look of this battalion. Let us see what\ngambits it can offer us.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m04_002: Hmm. The best place to experiment with gambits\nwould be Elissa Pass.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m04_003: Allow me to guide you there.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m05_001: Would you like some further education in the use\nof gambits, Your Majesty?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m05_002: <ICA>Agree.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m05_003: <ICB>Decline.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_m06_001: As you will. But I do advise gaining some experience\nwith them before our next match.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m01_001: This is the pass. Let us begin our training...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m02_001: AIIIEEE! Help! Someone!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m03_001: Hm?! What was that?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m04_001: My word! Some unfortunate soul is being attacked\nby wolves!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m05_001: Pull yourself together! Can you stand?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m05_002: Urgh... Yes, but...I hurt my leg.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m06_001: There will be no escaping with those injuries. Left\nto herself, she'll fall prey to the wolves.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m07_001: Allow me, Your Majesty! I'll make short work of\nthese beasts.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m07_002: Hold up! There's three wolves. If even one of them\nsurvives, it'll pounce.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08_001: Ngh... The wolves will pounce as a pack. We would\nhave to eliminate them all at once.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08_002: A fine opportunity for the battalion gambit of\n{SetColor=Gold}Disturbing Volley{SetColor=Default}!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08_003: It is capable of striking a line of {SetColor=Gold}three enemies\nsimultaneously{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08_004: What's more, it can {SetColor=Gold}immobilize{SetColor=Default} its targets for\n{SetColor=Gold}a short time{SetColor=Default}!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m08_005: Truly? That is perfect. Let us test this {SetColor=Gold}gambit {SetColor=Default}on\nthese foul wolves!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m09: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m09_001: Excellent! They appear to be locked in place.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m09_002: That is welcome news, but the battle is not yet won.\nLet us press the advantage and {SetColor=Gold}finish them{SetColor=Default} now!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m10: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m10_001: Those vile wolves are still stuck in place. Let us\nfinish them before it wears off.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m11: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m11_001: It's over. I see the value of these gambits now.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m11_002: They can only be employed {SetColor=Gold}so many times per battle{SetColor=Default}.\nThink carefully about the best time to use one.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m12: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m12_001: That was too close. I don't know how I can thank\nyou enough!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m12_002: Think nothing of it. I ought to thank you, in a way,\nfor the perfect training opportunity.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m12_003: Remain here, please, so that my people might see to\nyour safety and health.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m13: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m13_001: Your Majesty's gambit saved the day. Could I use\none too, if I were assigned a battalion?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m13_002: Yes...but {SetColor=Gold}cavalry units cannot have battalions{SetColor=Default}.\nYou would need to change your class first.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m13_003: So the trade-off to consider is a cavalry's superior\nmobility against a battalion's tactical possibilities.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_001_BM_m13_004: I shall take the balance into consideration as I\nprepare our forces for victory.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_008_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_008_m01_001: Guess we all oughta be workin' on {SetColor=Gold}passing our\ncertification exams{SetColor=Default} before the match.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_008_m01_002: Your Majesty, there is an {SetColor=Gold}armory{SetColor=Default} and {SetColor=Gold}item shop{SetColor=Default} in\nthe city where we can purchase any necessities.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_104_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_104_m01_001: What a curious bird...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_105_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_105_m01_001: What is this? A {SetColor=Gold}hint{SetColor=Default} about {SetColor=Gold}the battle to come{SetColor=Default}?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_105_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_105_m02_001: If you are unsure what to do in the preparation time\nbefore a match, then peruse the {SetColor=Gold}Adventure Journal{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m01_001: Hey, Queen Theodora!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_001: You and Bonaventure have been off working on\nsomething for a while. What were you up to?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_002: We were hearing reports concerning supply\nshortages. It could impact our {SetColor=Gold}combat readiness{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_003: Wow, is that part of a queen's duties? I figured you\ndelegated the boring stuff.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_004: Some are uneasy about my absence from the\nhomeland, even for the sake of our long-held dream.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_005: I must {SetColor=Gold}send supplies{SetColor=Default} to {SetColor=Gold}those who protect my people{SetColor=Default},\nso that they know my heart is always with Saramis.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_006: You mind if I help out with that?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m02_007: If Lilian is assisting, then naturally so am I.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m03_001: Ah, we are still lacking in some of the necessary\nsupplies. I shall go procure the remainder.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m04_001: Wait, Bonaventure. I will join you. I should like a\nbetter understanding of how supplies are gathered.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m04_002: As you wish. There are several methods, but they\nare best demonstrated outside Dagsion's walls.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_002_m04_003: Very well. Then let us be off.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m01_001: The most basic way to {SetColor=Gold}collect materials{SetColor=Default} is to travel\nabroad and {SetColor=Gold}search {SetColor=Default}your destination.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m01_002: But we require quite a lot of materials, and so it may\nbe wiser to {SetColor=Gold}deploy {SetColor=Default}our battalions to {SetColor=Gold}collect them{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m02_001: First, let us make our way over {SetColor=Gold}there{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m03_001: I have assigned the battalion I assembled to you.\nGive the order and it shall be {SetColor=Gold}deployed{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_GM_m04_001: They found an astonishing amount of supplies...\nWell done, everyone. Let us return.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m01_001: Nice! This oughta be everything we need.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m02_001: {SetColor=Gold}I will be acting as quartermaster{SetColor=Default} going forward.\nSpeak with me when you have supplies to send.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m03_001: Uh, Queen Theodora? Is it just me or are a lot of\nheads turning our way?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m04_001: Their queen is personally collecting supplies for her\npeople? She must really love them!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m04_002: I thought Saraminians were scarily intense, but\nmaybe they're nicer than I gave them credit for.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m04_003: It helps them feel more like regular folks—both the\naverage Saraminian and their queen!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m05_001: Your Majesty! The people of Dagsion seem to be\nrevising their opinion of us.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m05_002: Ohoho... This is an unexpected benefit.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_003_m05_003: I shall be sure to inform you of any new requests we\nhappen to receive.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01_001: Continuing to {SetColor=Gold}bolster our combat readiness{SetColor=Default} will no\ndoubt impress the people and {SetColor=Gold}enhance our renown{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01_002: That sounds like a worthwhile effort. Hrm?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01_003: There is something about {SetColor=Gold}that woman{SetColor=Default}... She has\nan air of assured competence to her.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01_004: Huh. You're right...there is something about her I\ncan't put my finger on.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m01_005: Perhaps she's a priest? Or some kind of diviner?\nShe may join us if we ask.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m02_001: That'd be great! Getting ourselves a diviner would\ntake some of the pressure off Bona.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m02_002: Perhaps Your Majesty might present her this {SetColor=Gold}gift{SetColor=Default}\nin order to {SetColor=Gold}recruit{SetColor=Default} her.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_103_m03_001: I shall consider it. Go on, the rest of you, and focus\non strengthening yourselves before the match.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m01_001: Let us gain {SetColor=Gold}allies{SetColor=Default} by gathering {SetColor=Gold}materials{SetColor=Default}, {SetColor=Gold}sending\nsupplies{SetColor=Default} home, and thereby raising our {SetColor=Gold}renown{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m01_002: If you are ever unsure how to accomplish these\nthings, I suggest perusing the {SetColor=Gold}Adventure Journal{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_Sop_m01_001: I heard you were a warrior, Queen Theodora.\nBut you seem very kind to me. I was so moved!
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_Sop_m01_002: The people of Saramis must be happy, having you\nsend them food they want. I'd like that too!
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_Sop_m01_003: Ack! Never mind! I didn't say that last part!
MID_LGA_1SEO_LG13_009_Sop_m01: <BLN>I'm jealous.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m02_001: I was certain we could get her to help us, but I should\nhave known it wouldn't be so easy.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m02_002: She's probably wary of folks from Saramis. Let's {SetColor=Gold}send\nsupplies{SetColor=Default} home to boost our {SetColor=Gold}renown{SetColor=Default}, then try again.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m03_001: Your Majesty, I come bearing good news.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m03_002: Bolstering our combat readiness will allow us to take\ncertification exams for several new classes.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m03_003: The first of these will be the {LowercaseNextLetter}{Variable=5}. Let\nus send supplies home that we may reach this goal.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m04_001: Excellent news! We are now eligible to take the\nexam for a new class.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m04_002: After this shall come the {LowercaseNextLetter}{Variable=5}. Let us\nsend supplies home that we may reach this goal.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m05_001: Excellent news! We are now eligible to take the\nexam for a new class.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_009_m05_002: I believe those are all the classes that will be on offer\nto us. Let us make the most of them.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m01_001: Hey, boss, wait till you hear what I found out!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m02_001: Knowing that it takes little to excite you, I would\nnevertheless hear your report.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m02_002: This place called the {SetColor=Gold}Vandahl Trading Company{SetColor=Default} has\nsome rare stuff I thought you might wanna check out.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m02_003: Ah, Talimun's shop {SetColor=Gold}by the port in lowtown{SetColor=Default}? Let us\nsee what Dagda's greatest trading house can offer.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m03_001: Now how does one reach {SetColor=Gold}lowtown{SetColor=Default} from here...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m03_002: If I recall correctly, I need only {SetColor=Gold}descend the stairs\nbeyond that arch{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Closed_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Closed_m01_001: This is not where I meant to go.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m04_001: Well now! If it isn't Her Majesty. Welcome!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m04_002: We have loads of rare goods. Go on, have a look!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Lys_m01_001: Goodness...this one is rather rare.
MID_LGA_1SEO_TG13_106_Lys_m01: <BLN>My goodness...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Tob_m01_001: What an axe! Gotta hand it to them—they carry\nquality work!
MID_LGA_1SEO_TG13_106_Tob_m01: <BLN>Whoa!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_Bon_m01_001: This could well be the linchpin of a new strategy...
MID_LGA_1SEO_TG13_106_Bon_m01: <BLN>If I had one of these...
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m05_001: Your Majesty, this place stocks all sorts of {SetColor=Gold}rare\nequipment{SetColor=Default} and accepts {SetColor=Gold}materials as payment{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m05_002: It may be a good place to spend the materials we\ngather across Dagda from {SetColor=Gold}searching{SetColor=Default} and {SetColor=Gold}deploying{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_106_m05_003: Hm. I shall take it into consideration. It may be\nprudent to {SetColor=Gold}strengthen our forces{SetColor=Default} here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_001: Your Majesty, I wonder if we have sufficient\nbattalions for the obstacles to come.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_002: Indeed. We have put them to good use collecting\nresources, but there is the next match to consider.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_003: The soldiers we brought with us from Saramis are\nalready assigned though. We can spare no more.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_004: Have we thought about expanding our ranks with\nlocal recruits?
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_005: There must be some who have been stirred by\nSaramis's victories in the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_006: I shall take the initiative to visit nearby settlements\nin person to {SetColor=Gold}recruit soldiers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_m01_007: Let us waste no time in beginning this work!
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m01_001: The village of {SetColor=Gold}Regia{SetColor=Default} strikes me as a good starting\npoint for our recruitment efforts.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m02_001: A village of this size is surely home to some {SetColor=Gold}residents\nof outstanding skill{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m02_002: I'd be happy to have whoever wants to join! Let's go\nsee about {SetColor=Gold}recruiting soldiers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m03_001: I must say, that was pleasantly successful for our first\nrecruitment drive.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_004_GM_m03_002: And as our {SetColor=Gold}renown improves{SetColor=Default}, we will doubtless\nattract {SetColor=Gold}soldiers of even greater skill{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_010_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_010_m01_001: Does Hong Hua intend to stay rooted to this spot\nuntil the day Bahr Vahn returns?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_010_m01_002: She would be a valuable ally. I ought to {SetColor=Gold}speak with\nher{SetColor=Default} on {SetColor=Gold}{DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}{SetColor=Default}, the day before the full moon.
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_010_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_LG13_010_m02_001: Hey, I figured out where the {SetColor=Gold}blacksmith{SetColor=Default} is, if you\never wanna {SetColor=Gold}repair {SetColor=Default}or {SetColor=Gold}refine {SetColor=Default}our {SetColor=Gold}weapons{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_011_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_011_m01_001: Where has Bahr Vahn fled to? We ought to {SetColor=Gold}search\nfor him{SetColor=Default} before he vanishes entirely.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_011_m01_002: He's been gravely injured, so there should be traces\nwe can follow.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c06_LG13_011_m01_003: But you know what they say about wounded beasts.\nDon't let your guard down even for a second.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_005_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_005_m01_001: Your Majesty, I have heard reports that our defenses\nin the homeland are somewhat lacking.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_005_m01_002: We might improve the situation by sending any\n{SetColor=Gold}surplus battalions{SetColor=Default} home to Saramis.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_005_m01_003: Speak to the {SetColor=Gold}transport chief{SetColor=Default} there and give the\ncommand to {SetColor=Gold}transfer soldiers{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_TG13_005_m01_004: Consider sending soldiers often. The more you send,\nthe more {SetColor=Gold}useful items {SetColor=Default}we shall receive in return.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_LG13_013_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_LG13_013_m01_001: {SetColor=Gold}Troy's shrine{SetColor=Default} is out past the Wandering Wood,\nisn't it?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_LG13_013_m01_004: I hear the forest there is dense and easy to get lost in.\nWe'll have to keep our wits about us.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_LG13_013_m01_003: It may be best to follow the roads as we make for the\n{SetColor=Gold}Tritopater Corridor{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_LG13_013_m01_002: Very well. Then that shall be our route.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_GM13_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_GM13_002_m01_001: I had not expected to encounter them today, but it is\ngood that we could find common ground.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_GM13_002_m01_002: Troy's shrine is not far, though we must first pass\nthrough the {SetColor=Gold}Wandering Wood{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m01_001: Yeesh, this place really lives up to its name.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m01_002: Odd. I feel that this is not quite the road I took the\nlast time I was here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m01_003: What do you mean?! How is that possible? And how\nare we supposed to find our way through?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m01_004: There is a method passed down among the forest\npeoples. We need only {SetColor=Gold}find the exit{SetColor=Default} to proceed.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c08_DN13_002_m02_001: Hm. We seem to have returned to where we began.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m01_001: {SetColor=Gold}Kunlun{SetColor=Default} is on the far west side of the Nysiades region.\nWe'll have to {SetColor=Gold}reach the Fezzan Gate{SetColor=Default} first.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m01_002: This will be a long journey, then. Let us take care\nto rest as needed.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m02_001: We're nearing a passage entrance. It's our best\nway into the village of {SetColor=Gold}Kunlun{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_GM13_003_m02_002: But powerful monsters make their home in that\npassage, so be ready for anything.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01_001: So this is the legendary White Egg. Or should I say\nthe village of Kunlun?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01_002: Look at all this stuff! I'm so excited, my teeth\nmight fall out.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01_003: Hoho! I admit that I can hardly contain my\nexcitement either.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01_004: Agreed. I would like to {SetColor=Gold}tour the village{SetColor=Default} and see how\nour kin live.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_LG13_015_m01_005: Go see {SetColor=Gold}Zenon {SetColor=Default}once you're ready to move on.\nHe should have a sensor for you.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_DN13_004_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_DN13_004_m01_001: Our objective is a metal called {SetColor=Gold}epimenium{SetColor=Default}. Let us\ngo farther in and find a sample.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_DN13_004_m01_002: The device is meant to {SetColor=Gold}react more strongly{SetColor=Default} as we\ndraw near to what we seek.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_DN13_004_Closed_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c09_DN13_004_Closed_m01_001: There seems to be nothing. Perhaps you should\nsearch someplace else.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m01_001: Long departed to meet with Anatolia and her clan\nbut said that he wishes Your Majesty good fortune.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m01_002: Understood. Let us renew our efforts to claim victory\nin the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m01_003: We may have our own reunion with Anatolia's clan\nin the main matches.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m02_001: <DLG>If you lend Anatolia the Trafalgar, you will not be able to traverse the\nseas until Seftim 21. Do you really want to lend her the ship?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m02_002: <ICA>Yes
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m02_003: <ICB>No
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m03_001: Thank you. We will depart as soon as our\npreparations are complete.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m04_001: I understand. If you change your mind, please speak\nwith me again.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m05_001: Theodora, are you now able to lend me the ship?
MID_LGA_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m05: <BLN>Are you prepared now?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m06_001: <DLG>If you lend Anatolia the Trafalgar, you will not be able to traverse the\nseas until Seftim 21. Do you really want to lend her the ship?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m06_002: <ICA>Yes
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m06_003: <ICB>No
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m07_001: Thank you. We will depart as soon as our\npreparations are complete.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c10_LG13_016_m08_001: I understand. If you change your mind, please speak\nwith me again.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_017_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_017_m01_001: The Trafalgar, which you lent to Anatolia, has been returned.\n(You can now traverse sea locations.)
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01_001: I am curious, Your Majesty. What was this loose end\nyou mentioned?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01_002: My audience with Yu Phas's daughter, Aurora.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01_003: I meant to speak with her while we are here in\nDagsion, and that has not yet happened.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01_004: Considering the obstacles we have faced thus far,\nit may be easier said than done.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_018_m01_005: Regardless, it is worth a last visit to {SetColor=Gold}Aurora's temple{SetColor=Default}\nin hopes of securing an audience.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_Kai_Closed_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_Kai_Closed_m01_001: Not that way, Theodora.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m01_001: If I go with you, will I finally be able to meet\nwith Aurora?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m01_002: Absolutely. Just trust me and come on!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m01_003: Very well. Show me the way, and be quick about it.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m01_004: Alright. We just gotta go downstairs to the shopping\narcade, then {SetColor=Gold}past the item shop to the street's end{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02_001: Do not test me, Cai. This path is clearly impassable.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02_002: It's alright. See? I've got the key right here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02_003: What?! Why would you have such a thing?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02_004: Well... Let's not worry about that.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_LG13_019_m02_005: Hmph... First that mysterious spear and now this?\nJust who is he?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_DN13_006_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c11_DN13_006_m01_001: Just {SetColor=Gold}keep going down that passage{SetColor=Default}...and watch\nwhere you step.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01_001: I am surprised we received permission to use the\nGate of the Gods at Yu Phas's temple.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01_002: I find it not so surprising. But I am happy to have\nanother connection with our goddess.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01_003: About time we get to walk through the front doors\nof Yu Phas's temple!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01_004: Still, there is no time for rejoicing. We must prepare\nfor our battle with the Mosa.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_m01_005: When the day comes, be ready to return to Megaira\nvia the {SetColor=Gold}Gate of the Gods{SetColor=Default} in {SetColor=Gold}Yu Phas's temple{SetColor=Default}!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m01_001: I've been keeping watch here since the fort fell, and\nI'm certain the Mosa don't know of this path.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m01_002: May Your Majesty make a swift return to Megaira\nand lead our forces to recapture the fortress!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m02_001: Apparently, several thousand Mosa soldiers used this\nroute to storm the fort the other day.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m02_002: I worry they might have reinforcements coming.\nWe'll keep an eye out from here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m03_001: Fort Zanbar's gates are shut tight for the moment.\nWe've heard nothing but silence from inside.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_020_GM_m03_002: If anything changes, we'll send word at once. Please\nreturn to Megaira for now, Your Majesty.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_022_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_022_m01_001: We do not have the luxury of time. It would be best\nto make for Megaira at once.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_022_m01_002: Though I do find this place intriguing. I may as well\nhave a look around as I {SetColor=Gold}seek the exit{SetColor=Default}.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_GM13_005_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_GM13_005_m01_001: From here at Ahm Lu, a bygone road crosses Lake\nBrontes and leads to the way to Megaira.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_GM13_005_m01_002: It is an old road built during the Damascar period.\nIf we follow it, we shall be at Megaira soon enough.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_GM13_005_m01_003: You seem to know the area well. Fond memories of\nsneaking into Yu Phas's temple, I take it?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_GM13_005_m01_004: Indeed. Though who was it that told me of the path\nin my youth? Was it Troy?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_023_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_023_m01_001: Things seem rather hectic inside the royal palace.\nThough I suppose that is to be expected.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_LG13_023_m01_002: When you are ready, speak to {SetColor=Gold}Kumos{SetColor=Default}, and we will\nconvene the war council.